; 30-repl-functions: function values at the REPL, shown as "=> value".  A line is one S-expression of its items,
; so a lone function is called with nothing: a function of formals gives itself back (a partial with none bound),
; one of no formals runs, a built-in runs ((+) is 0, (print) prints a line); a call whose value is a function of no
; formals is called again.  Two items on a line are a call of the first.  Errors show "=> Error:" and the trace
; (stderr).  Multi-line definitions (the open brackets shown).  (This comment is a line of its own: NIL.)
(fn {x} {* x 2})
(fun {add a b} {+ a b})
add
(add 1)
((add 1) 2)
(add 1 2 3)
(eq 1)
(substring "hi")
(fexpr {x} {x})
+
print
(print :printed)
(def {f0} (fn {} {:f0-ran}))
f0
(print f0)
(fun {mk0} {fn {} {:made-and-called}})
(mk0)
(print (mk0))
